Rules:
- Prefer needs_review over false exclusions when evidence is weak.
- Use public for government/CHU/public hospital operators.
- Use individual for solo practitioners / cabinets.
- Use unrelated for shops, hotels, schools, spas, and non-treatment businesses.
- Use eligible_candidate only when evidence supports a non-government addiction-treatment center.
- `addiction_treatment_mission` means the facility genuinely provides treatment for alcohol,
  drug, and/or behavioral addictions — NOT that addiction is its primary, main, or only
  specialty. A general psychiatric hospital or multidisciplinary facility can still be
  "confirmed" if it runs its own actual addiction-treatment program alongside other services.
  Merely mentioning addiction, offering referrals elsewhere, or treating unrelated
  psychiatric/mental-health conditions is NOT sufficient for "confirmed". Use "unknown" when
  evidence is insufficient either way — do not use "contradicted" just because you found nothing;
  reserve "contradicted" for evidence that actively rules out addiction treatment.
- `inpatient_treatment` / `residential_accommodation`: true only when a verified source
  explicitly confirms clients can stay overnight / live at the facility during treatment, for
  THIS facility specifically (not a parent organization's other locations). `medical_detox`:
  true only when a verified source explicitly describes supervised/medical withdrawal
  management. Use null — never a guess — whenever the evidence is missing, ambiguous, or only
  describes outpatient/day-program services. A false claim here is worse than leaving it null.
- Every `true` value for inpatient_treatment, residential_accommodation, or medical_detox MUST
  have a matching evidence item (same "field") with a real quote and a real, verifiable
  source_url — never assert one of these without citing exactly where it came from.
- `ownership_status`: use "confirmed_non_government" ONLY when a verified source states an actual
  ownership/operator FACT for THIS specific facility — e.g. it is operated by a named registered
  NGO, charity, foundation, association, religious organization, or private company, or an
  explicit acquisition/parent-company/ownership-transfer statement. Use "confirmed_government"
  only when a verified source confirms it is run by a government ministry, municipal authority,
  public hospital system, or other state body. Never use either "confirmed_*" value merely
  because the facility's own NAME sounds private, religious, or nonprofit, or because of a
  business-suffix pattern (e.g. a name containing "Oy", "ry", "Foundation") with no other
  evidence — that is a guess, not a fact, and must be "probable_non_government" or "unknown"
  instead. Use "unknown" when there is no usable ownership evidence at all. Every
  "confirmed_non_government"/"confirmed_government" value MUST have a matching evidence item
  (field "ownership_status") with a real quote stating the actual ownership fact and a real,
  verifiable source_url.
- Return JSON only. No markdown fences. No results array wrapper.
